    best_season = 'October to April (cooler months)',
    summary = 'The pyramids, the Nile and 5,000 years of history, from pharaohs'' tombs to medieval Islamic Cairo.',
    history = 'Ancient Egypt united around 3100 BC and built the Giza pyramids around 2500 BC. Later it was ruled by Greeks, Romans, Arab caliphates, the Mamluks and the Ottomans, and was under British influence before full independence in the 20th century.',
    culture = 'Life follows the Nile, and Cairo is the busy cultural capital of the Arab world for film, music and literature. Hospitality is central, and tea and shisha in a street café are a daily ritual.',
    beliefs = 'About 90% of Egyptians are Sunni Muslims and around 10% are Coptic Christians, one of the oldest Christian communities in the world. During Ramadan many people fast from dawn to sunset.',
    etiquette = 'Dress conservatively, especially in mosques, where women should cover their hair. Use your right hand to eat and give things. Bargaining is expected in markets, and small tips (baksheesh) are part of daily life. Ask before photographing people.',
