    plug_types = 'A, C',
    best_season = 'May to September (dry season in the Andes)',
    summary = 'Inca citadels above the clouds, high Andean valleys and a capital that is one of the world''s great food cities.',
    history = 'Peru was home to cultures such as the Nazca, Moche and Chimú long before the Inca Empire, centred on Cusco, became the largest in the Americas in the 15th century. Spanish conquistadors arrived in 1532, and Peru declared independence in 1821.',
    culture = 'Indigenous Andean traditions blend with Spanish, African and Asian influences, which shows most clearly in the food: ceviche, lomo saltado and Nikkei (Japanese-Peruvian) cooking.',
    beliefs = 'Most Peruvians are Catholic, often mixed with Andean beliefs such as honouring Pachamama (Mother Earth) and the apus (mountain spirits). Inti Raymi, the Inca festival of the sun, is celebrated in Cusco every June.',
